<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahvaz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahvaz is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karun-river">Karun River</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> province. An important town of the Sasanian and early Islamic periods, it was sacked by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanj">Zanj</a> rebels in the 9th century. It revived in the 20th century as a centre of Iran's oil industry and was heavily fought over in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran-iraq-war">Iran–Iraq War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahvaz.jpg" alt="Ahvaz" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eeehhssaannn2 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PoleSefid.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
